{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4b9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":183,"recorded_at":1780531400000361,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d33e-8eef-79c0-9e43-2d68d010e9d4"},"task_id":"01a0d33e-8eef-79c0-9e43-2d68d010e9d4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d33e-8eef-79c0-9e43-2d68d010e9d4","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-7-1\",\n  \"command\": \"/Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board q 'get(TASK-260924-3n78rv){full}' 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(d,indent=1)[:12000])\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Get full task JSON\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\n \\\"ac\\\": \\\"Planning decisions are driven through production entries with whole-domain oracles over strategy x profile x item class; injected instruction-like or reply-like visible text never gains authority at any entry; every rule has a narrowing killed by its named test run alone.\\\",\\n \\\"assignee\\\": \\\"[implementer] developer (muse)\\\",\\n \\\"blockedBy\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260830-1jmmqn\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"blocks\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260830-1esv6u\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"checklist\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Planning decisions by whole-domain oracle through the production planning entry: strategy (5 incl. archive_only and continuation_context) x profile (5) x item class (every Canonical Event kind and content-block type) yields exactly the expected disposition and reason set per pinned SPEC v0.7.0 \\\\u00a713.14.1/\\\\u00a713.14.2 (10385-10393, 10548-10570); continuation_context is explicitly non-native; historical tools are inert and incomplete calls become aborted history; source usage never becomes target accounting\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Authority is never escalated: VisibleMigrationProjection has exactly authority=user_context (10808-10812) and visible text comes only from typed escaped fields; foreign instructions stay low-authority history; for every injected instruction-like, reply-like, control-token-like and authorization-like text at every event position and every entry, the plan never emits an assistant reply, system instruction, tool call or authorization; an independent oracle classifies authority\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Axis inventory (strategy, profile, event kind, content-block type, text payload class, position) with generated ranges for unbounded text payloads plus a structural argument that authority is decided by type, never by text content; importer outcome grid keyed (package, entry, input) with moved classes named; reuse internal/clonefidelity and internal/cloneplan (landed checkpoints); task_delta, no registry edit\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot \\\\u2014 never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio \\\\u2014 `n of m AC rows driven` \\\\u2014 and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant \\\\u2014 the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Lint clean\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Tests green\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read \\\\u2014 positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"If review does not accept the work \\\\u2014 verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"children\\\": [],\\n \\\"created\\\": \\\"2026-09-23T22:49:11Z\\\",\\n \\\"derivedBlockedBy\\\": [],\\n \\\"derivedBlocks\\\": [],\\n \\\"description\\\": \\\"Split from TASK-260830-1jmmqn on 2026-09-24 (one attack surface per leaf). Plan the pair-neutral target projection: strategy and profile selection, item mappings with expected dispositions and reasons, checkpoint message authority (visible text from typed escaped fields is low-authority user context, never an assistant reply, system instruction or authorization; pinned SPEC v0.7.0 ~10392, ~10587, ~10812), inactive tools/instructions as low-authority history, token metadata, and vendor importer strategies. Builds on the Projection Plan schema leaf. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\\\",\\n \\\"estimate\\\": {\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"estimated\\\",\\n  \\\"scale\\\": {\\n   \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fibonacci\\\",\\n   \\\"number\\\": 8\\n  }\\n },\\n \\\"id\\\": \\\"TASK-260924-3n78rv\\\",\\n \\\"integrationCheckpointed\\\": false,\\n \\\"isAdvisoryBlocked\\\": false,\\n \\\"isBlocked\\\": false,\\n \\\"name\\\": \\\"implement-projection-planning-and-authority-rules\\\",\\n \\\"notes\\\": \\\"spawn workload selection: class=implementation source=explicit policy=spawn.workload_classes pair=muse/muse-spark/max pair_source=explicit match=recommended_rank_1 snapshot=sha256:12703c4ea40d4bba69ef5e32089d666fbbcc482e0bd7b83006fefd0daca183ea rationale=\\\\\\\"Chain 3 next leaf: projection planning + authority-by-type rules (split from 1jmmqn), after 1jmmqn checkpoint 5bfbc78; muse max.\\\\\\\"\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: muse via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[muse,codex,claude], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\\\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260924-aa8f5f, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (muse) (run=RUN-260924-aa8f5f)\\\\nrefresh-candidate attempted 3x, INTERNAL_ERROR change_request_checkpoint_conflict persisting recovery intent; only retained replay in base-refresh belongs to another story branch (dab37c0). Proceeding with implementation; will retry refresh before handoff per brief.\\\\nProducer evidence attached: results 18/18, conformance matrix, evidence tar 25KB. Full suite green 47/47 at -p 2; parallel reds proven load flakes (sessquery probe green both sides, sessstate fails identically on base, zero dep edge). refresh-candidate still refuses: stale recovery intent pins mid-work tree 8c0fc7d, current 2530f4d; --replay-resolutions with the conflict-free template also refused. Attempting handoff; if CR construction enforces trunk descent the stale intent needs operator clearing.\\\\nspawn run child final message (run=RUN-260924-aa8f5f, tools=203 patches=50 failed=4):\\\\nTASK-260924-3n78rv (implement projection planning and authority rules) is ready for review \\\\u2014 board status `to-review`, all 14 checklist items checked, three outcome resources attached.\\\\n\\\\nWhat was built: new package `internal/cloneplanning` ([doc.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-21bxa3/worktree/internal/cloneplanning/doc.go)) with 8 production entries \\\\u2014 strategy/profile selection, event\\\\u2192item classification, per-item disposition planning, session planning with predicted counts, visible-text projection with `authority=user_context`, and a zero target-effects fold. Candidate is 16 new paths, uncommitted; no landed file edited, no registry edit. Derivation R-ARCH\\\\u2026R-SEL-P with pinned spec quotes, axis inventory, and bounds are in [TRACEABILITY.md](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent