{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c64f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":386,"recorded_at":1780531400000767,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"call_id":"call_01a0d33edaa872f681204d09d3dd7bfc","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneplanning/doc.go`.\n1|package cloneplanning\n2|\n3|// This package plans the pair-neutral target projection: strategy\n4|// and profile selection, per-item expected dispositions with reason\n5|// sets, checkpoint visible-text authority, historical-tool\n6|// inertness, and source/target usage separation. It is the third\n7|// leaf of the fidelity-projection-and-validation-contracts story:\n8|// planning semantics only. Closed shapes stay owned by the schema\n9|// siblings (internal/clonefidelity dispositions/reasons,\n10|// internal/cloneplan Projection Plan and Projected Object Manifest,\n11|// internal/clonebundle capture/canonical contracts,\n12|// internal/cloneproject G1 normalization); this package decides,\n13|// never re-validates, their shapes.\n14|//\n15|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0,\n16|// Section 13.14.1 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md, lines\n17|// 10385-10393: event kinds, content blocks, \"Historical tools are\n18|// inert; incomplete calls become aborted history\", \"Foreign\n19|// instructions are low-authority history, foreign encrypted/signed\n20|// reasoning is opaque-preserved, and source usage is not target\n21|// accounting\") and Section 13.14.2 (lines 10548-10570:\n22|// dispositions, reasons, profiles, strategies, \"Continuation\n23|// context is explicitly non-native historical fidelity\"), the\n24|// Projection Plan 1.0.0 table (strategy/profile four-lists), the\n25|// projection-plan adapter contract (\"archive_only is forbidden\",\n26|// line 3841), and Migration Checkpoint VisibleMigrationProjection\n27|// (lines 10808-10812: \"authority=user_context\", \"never an\n28|// assistant reply, system instruction, or authorization\",\n29|// \"Visible text comes from typed escaped fields and is user\n30|// context, never an assistant reply or control instruction\").\n31|//\n32|// Production entries: SelectStrategy, SelectProfile, ClassifyItem,\n33|// PlanItem, PlanSession, ProjectVisibleText, EscapeVisibleText, and\n34|// PlanTargetEffects. Every rule is driven through these entries by\n35|// a whole-domain oracle written in the tests from the derivation in\n36|// TRACEABILITY.md; every gate ships a narrowing mutant killed by\n37|// its named test run alone (see\n38|// testdata/mutant_harness.py). Authority is decided by type, never\n39|// by text: the visible authority is one constant, the item\n40|// classifier admits closed vocabularies only, and the structural\n41|// test pins that shape with control plants.\n42|//\n43|// Reuse, not fork: strategy/profile/disposition/reason/event-kind/\n44|// block vocabularies delegate to internal/clonefidelity,\n45|// internal/cloneplan, and internal/clonebundle; target-branch\n46|// admission (unstable refusal, maximal-safe completeness) stays\n47|// with clonesnap.AdmitForTarget and the clonebundle G2 gates;\n48|// G1 tool/instruction/usage folds stay with internal/cloneproject\n49|// (this package consumes the completed/aborted and\n50|// encrypted/signed facts it lands); character measures and uint53\n51|// come from internal/environ and internal/scalar. The fact names\n52|// ClassifyItem reads (resolution, protection) follow cloneproject's\n53|// landed registry; value vocabularies are gated here.\n54|//\n55|// Stated bounds (sibling scope or spec-silent, not waived): target\n56|// operation synthesis from dispositions; source-condition reasons\n57|// (source_not_persisted, source_truncated, source_corrupt) and\n58|// target-condition reasons (target_schema_constraint,\n59|// target_size_limit, target_version_gate, credential_excluded,\n60|// secret_policy, derived_index_rebuilt) need inputs the item axis\n61|// does not carry; capability-gated degradation beyond the tool and\n62|// subagent importer classes; per-kind text-field extraction (the\n63|// visible entry takes extracted typed texts); the full Migration\n64|// Checkpoint Build/Decode shape (a future leaf seals it from the\n65|// authority value pinned here); cross-package payload fact-name\n66|// renames past the grep pin. See TRACEABILITY.md.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c651","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":387,"recorded_at":1780531400000769,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"call_id":"call_01a0d33edb86730d9f2345bf7e9e616b","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneplanning/strategy.go`.\n1|package cloneplanning\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/cloneplan\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// This file selects the projection strategy and profile branch.\n8|// Selection is pair-neutral: it consumes only resolved boolean\n9|// signals and closed names, never concrete environment identities\n10|// or manifest bytes. Target-branch admission (the unstable refusal\n11|// and maximal-safe completeness) stays owned by\n12|// clonesnap.AdmitForTarget; SelectProfile routes the branch, the\n13|// caller admits the manifest under the returned profile. Strategy\n14|// and profile spellings stay owned by the internal/clonefidelity\n15|// and internal/cloneplan vocabularies; the literals below quote\n16|// them, and the agreement test pins the quote.\n17|\n18|// Branch is the projection branch a profile selects: target or\n19|// archive. Archive carries no Projection Plan (Section 13.14.2:\n20|// the archive report is targetless, and the projection-plan\n21|// contract forbids archive_only).\n22|type Branch string\n23|\n24|const (\n25|\t// BranchTarget carries a Projection Plan.\n26|\tBranchTarget Branch = \"target\"\n27|\t// BranchArchive carries no plan: G0/G1 closure only.\n28|\tBranchArchive Branch = \"archive\"\n29|)\n30|\n31|// Section 13.14.2 strategy spellings, quoted from the\n32|// internal/clonefidelity owner.\n33|const (\n34|\tstrategyNativeRewrite = \"same_environment_native_rewrite\"\n35|\tstrategyNativeWriter  = \"target_native_writer\"\n36|\tstrategyOfficial      = \"target_official_import\"\n37|\tstrategyContinuation  = \"continuation_context\"\n38|\tstrategyArchive       = \"archive_only\"\n39|)\n40|\n41|// profileArchive quotes the archive profile spelling.\n42|const profileArchive = \"archive_only\"\n43|\n44|// SelectStrategy selects one Section 13.14.2 strategy from resolved\n45|// pair signals. sameEnvironment reports whether source and target\n46|// share one native environment; officialImport reports whether the\n47|// target adapter offers the official_import capability;\n48|// continuation reports an explicit continuation-context request;\n49|// archive reports an explicit archive-only request. Priority is\n50|// archive, then continuation, then the pair/capability arm: an\n51|// explicit archive request always wins, an explicit continuation\n52|// request wins over the pair, a cross-environment pair with the\n53|// vendor importer uses target_official_import, a cross-environment\n54|// pair without it uses target_native_writer, and a same-environment\n55|// pair uses same_environment_native_rewrite.\n56|func SelectStrategy(sameEnvironment, officialImport, continuation, archive bool) (string, error) {\n57|\tif archive {\n58|\t\treturn strategyArchive, nil\n59|\t}\n60|\tif continuation {\n61|\t\treturn strategyContinuation, nil\n62|\t}\n63|\tif !sameEnvironment {\n64|\t\tif officialImport {\n65|\t\t\treturn strategyOfficial, nil\n66|\t\t}\n67|\t\treturn strategyNativeWriter, nil\n68|\t}\n69|\treturn strategyNativeRewrite, nil\n70|}\n71|\n72|// SelectProfile validates one requested profile and routes its\n73|// branch. archive_only routes the archive branch, which carries no\n74|// plan. The four plan profiles route the target branch; the caller\n75|// admits the capture manifest under the returned profile through\n76|// the landed clonesnap.AdmitForTarget gate. Anything else refuses\n77|// through the plan-profile gate.\n78|func SelectProfile(requested string) (Branch, string, error) {\n79|\tif requested == profileArchive {\n80|\t\treturn BranchArchive, requested, nil\n81|\t}\n82|\tif !cloneplan.ValidPlanProfile(requested) {\n83|\t\treturn \"\", \"\", invalid(\"projection profile %q is outside strict_exact|maximal_safe|compact|messages_only|archive_only\", requested)\n84|\t}\n85|\treturn BranchTarget, requested, nil\n86|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c653","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":388,"recorded_at":1780531400000771,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"call_id":"call_01a0d33edc7e766a83602b973bee9dc7","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneplanning/item.go`.\n1|package cloneplanning\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonebundle\"\n5|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/cloneproject\"\n6|)\n7|\n8|// This file bridges decoded Canonical Events to planning items.\n9|// Classification is by closed vocabularies only: the event kind\n10|// plus the completed/aborted tool resolution and the\n11|// encrypted/signed opaque protection. Every other payload text is\n12|// ignored (the sweep proves adversarial payload text cannot change\n13|// the item), and every unknown fact value refuses. The fact names\n14|// (resolution, protection) follow cloneproject's landed registry;\n15|// the completed/aborted spellings reference its exported statuses\n16|// so a rename breaks the build, and the protection spellings are\n17|// pinned against its source by the composition test.\n18|\n19|// Item is one plannable source class: exactly one of Kind (a\n20|// Canonical Event kind) or Block (a content-block type) is set.\n21|// Resolution carries the folded tool resolution for tool_call and\n22|// tool_result only; Protection carries the opaque protection for\n23|// opaque_reasoning (required) and opaque_event (admitted, the\n24|// unknown-native reason does not vary by it). Content blocks carry\n25|// neither fact: blocks have no protection member.\n26|type Item struct {\n27|\tKind       string\n28|\tBlock      string\n29|\tResolution string\n30|\tProtection string\n31|}\n32|\n33|// Protection spellings, quoted from cloneproject's landed\n34|// none|encrypted|signed envelope vocabulary.\n35|const (\n36|\tprotectionEncrypted = \"encrypted\"\n37|\tprotectionSigned    = \"signed\"\n38|)\n39|\n40|// toolKinds admit the folded resolution fact.\n41|var toolKinds = map[string]bool{\n42|\t\"tool_call\":   true,\n43|\t\"tool_result\": true,\n44|}\n45|\n46|// validResolution reports whether the value is an admitted\n47|// resolution: absent or one of cloneproject's folded statuses.\n48|func validResolution(value string) bool {\n49|\treturn value == \"\" || value == cloneproject.StatusCompleted || value == cloneproject.StatusAborted\n50|}\n51|\n52|// validProtection reports whether the value is an admitted\n53|// protection: absent, encrypted, or signed.\n54|func validProtection(value string) bool {\n55|\treturn value == \"\" || value == protectionEncrypted || value == protectionSigned\n56|}\n57|\n58|// checkItem validates one caller-supplied item: exactly one class\n59|// member set, closed kind/block vocabularies, and kind-gated fact\n60|// admission with required facts present.\n61|func checkItem(item Item) error {\n62|\tif (item.Kind == \"\") == (item.Block == \"\") {\n63|\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item sets kind and block together or neither; exactly one class member is required\")\n64|\t}\n65|\tif item.Kind != \"\" {\n66|\t\tif !clonebundle.ValidEventKind(item.Kind) {\n67|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item kind %q is not a Canonical Event kind\", item.Kind)\n68|\t\t}\n69|\t} else {\n70|\t\tif !clonebundle.ValidContentBlockType(item.Block) {\n71|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item block %q is not a content-block type\", item.Block)\n72|\t\t}\n73|\t}\n74|\tif !validResolution(item.Resolution) {\n75|\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item resolution %q is outside completed|aborted\", item.Resolution)\n76|\t}\n77|\tif !validProtection(item.Protection) {\n78|\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item protection %q is outside encrypted|signed\", item.Protection)\n79|\t}\n80|\tif item.Block != \"\" {\n81|\t\tif item.Resolution != \"\" {\n82|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item block carries a tool resolution; blocks carry no resolution fact\")\n83|\t\t}\n84|\t\tif item.Protection != \"\" {\n85|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item block carries a protection fact; blocks carry no protection fact\")\n86|\t\t}\n87|\t\treturn nil\n88|\t}\n89|\tif toolKinds[item.Kind] {\n90|\t\tif item.Resolution == \"\" {\n91|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item kind %q requires its completed|aborted resolution\", item.Kind)\n92|\t\t}\n93|\t} else if item.Resolution != \"\" {\n94|\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item kind %q carries a tool resolution; only tool_call and tool_result admit one\", item.Kind)\n95|\t}\n96|\tif item.Kind == \"opaque_reasoning\" {\n97|\t\tif item.Protection == \"\" {\n98|\t\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item kind opaque_reasoning requires its encrypted|signed protection\")\n99|\t\t}\n100|\t} else if item.Kind == \"opaque_event\" {\n101|\t\treturn nil\n102|\t} else if item.Protection != \"\" {\n103|\t\treturn invalid(\"projection item kind %q carries a protection fact; only opaque kinds admit one\", item.Kind)\n104|\t}\n105|\treturn nil\n106|}\n107|\n108|// ClassifyItem bridges one decoded Canonical Event to its planning\n109|// item: the kind plus the closed resolution/protection facts when\n110|// the landed payload carries them. Unknown fact values refuse;\n111|// every other payload member is ignored by type (the item has no\n112|// text field to carry it).\n113|func ClassifyItem(event clonebundle.CanonicalEvent) (Item, error) {\n114|\tif !clonebundle.ValidEventKind(event.Kind) {\n115|\t\treturn Item{}, invalid(\"projection item kind %q is not a Canonical Event kind\", event.Kind)\n116|\t}\n117|\tresolution, err := closedFact(event.Payload, \"resolution\")\n118|\tif err != nil {\n119|\t\treturn Item{}, err\n120|\t}\n121|\tprotection, err := closedFact(event.Payload, \"protection\")\n122|\tif err != nil {\n123|\t\treturn Item{}, err\n124|\t}\n125|\titem := Item{Kind: event.Kind, Resolution: resolution, Protection: protection}\n126|\tif err := checkItem(item); err != nil {\n127|\t\treturn Item{}, err\n128|\t}\n129|\treturn item, nil\n130|}\n131|\n132|// closedFact reads one optional closed-vocabulary payload fact. An\n133|// absent member maps to absent; a present member must be a string,\n134|// and its admission is decided by the caller's vocabulary gate.\n135|func closedFact(payload map[string]any, name string) (string, error) {\n136|\traw, present := payload[name]\n137|\tif !present || raw == nil {\n138|\t\treturn \"\", nil\n139|\t}\n140|\tvalue, ok := raw.(string)\n141|\tif !ok {\n142|\t\treturn \"\", invalid(\"projection item fact %q is not a string\", name)\n143|\t}\n144|\treturn value, nil\n145|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c655","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":389,"recorded_at":1780531400000773,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"call_id":"call_01a0d33edd47727d824c7fb2eb5d18ab","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneplanning/plan.go`.\n1|package cloneplanning\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"sort\"\n5|\n6|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonefidelity\"\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/cloneproject\"\n8|)\n9|\n10|// This file plans per-item expected dispositions with reason sets\n11|// and folds planned sessions to predicted counts. The strategy arm\n12|// decides the base mapping, the profile overlay refines it, and\n13|// reasons compose as sorted sets. The planner never emits\n14|// synthesized (synthesized rows have no source object) or\n15|// unrecoverable (planned canonical items exist), and never plans\n16|// the archive branch. Disposition and reason spellings quote the\n17|// internal/clonefidelity owner; the agreement test pins the quote.\n18|\n19|// Mapping is one planned item: its expected disposition and sorted\n20|// reason set. Exact mappings carry no reason.\n21|type Mapping struct {\n22|\tDisposition string\n23|\tReasons     []string\n24|}\n25|\n26|// Disposition spellings, quoted from the internal/clonefidelity\n27|// owner.\n28|const (\n29|\tdispositionExact           = \"exact\"\n30|\tdispositionSemantic        = \"semantic\"\n31|\tdispositionSummarized      = \"summarized\"\n32|\tdispositionOpaquePreserved = \"opaque_preserved\"\n33|\tdispositionOmitted         = \"omitted\"\n34|)\n35|\n36|// Reason spellings, quoted from the internal/clonefidelity owner.\n37|const (\n38|\treasonTargetNoEquivalent   = \"target_no_equivalent\"\n39|\treasonForeignEncrypted     = \"foreign_encrypted_payload\"\n40|\treasonForeignSigned        = \"foreign_signature_unverifiable\"\n41|\treasonOfficialImporterLoss = \"official_importer_loss\"\n42|\treasonGraphFlattened       = \"graph_flattened\"\n43|\treasonUnsafePending        = \"unsafe_pending_action\"\n44|\treasonOperatorPolicy       = \"operator_policy\"\n45|\treasonUnsupportedMedia     = \"unsupported_media_type\"\n46|\treasonUnknownNative        = \"unknown_native_event\"\n47|\treasonTargetContextLimit   = \"target_context_limit\"\n48|)\n49|\n50|// Profile spellings, quoted from the internal/clonefidelity owner.\n51|const (\n52|\tprofileStrictExact = \"strict_exact\"\n53|\tprofileMaximalSafe = \"maximal_safe\"\n54|\tprofileCompact     = \"compact\"\n55|\tprofileMessages    = \"messages_only\"\n56|)\n57|\n58|// completeToolKinds degrade under the vendor importer: the\n59|// importer's native tool history is lossy.\n60|var completeToolKinds = map[string]bool{\n61|\t\"tool_call\":                true,\n62|\t\"tool_result\":              true,\n63|\t\"tool_definition_snapshot\": true,\n64|}\n65|\n66|// subagentKinds flatten under the vendor importer: the subagent\n67|// graph does not survive official import.\n68|var subagentKinds = map[string]bool{\n69|\t\"subagent_started\":   true,\n70|\t\"subagent_completed\": true,\n71|}\n72|\n73|// messageKinds survive messages_only at the event level.\n74|var messageKinds = map[string]bool{\n75|\t\"user_message\":      true,\n76|\t\"assistant_message\": true,\n77|}\n78|\n79|// messageBlocks survive messages_only at the block level:\n80|// text and structured message content plus the redaction marker,\n81|// which preserves the redaction exactly.\n82|var messageBlocks = map[string]bool{\n83|\t\"text\":     true,\n84|\t\"json\":     true,\n85|\t\"redacted\": true,\n86|}\n87|\n88|// mediaBlocks are message content the messages_only profile cannot\n89|// carry: the target shows text messages, not media.\n90|var mediaBlocks = map[string]bool{\n91|\t\"image\":         true,\n92|\t\"audio\":         true,\n93|\t\"document\":      true,\n94|\t\"resource_link\": true,\n95|}\n96|\n97|// maxSessionItems bounds one planned session: the Projection Plan\n98|// 1.0.0 table carries item_mappings[1..1000000].\n99|const maxSessionItems = 1000000\n100|\n101|// PlanItem plans one item's expected disposition with its reason\n102|// set under the strategy and profile. Unknown strategies,\n103|// profiles, or item classes refuse; the archive strategy or\n104|// profile refuses (archive carries no plan); strict_exact refuses\n105|// every non-exact item.\n106|func PlanItem(strategy, profile string, item Item) (Mapping, error) {\n107|\tif !clonefidelity.ValidStrategy(strategy) {\n108|\t\treturn Mapping{}, invalid(\"projection strategy %q is outside the Section 13.14.2 vocabulary\", strategy)\n109|\t}\n110|\tif strategy == strategyArchive || profile == profileArchive {\n111|\t\treturn Mapping{}, invalid(\"projection strategy %q with profile %q names the archive branch, which carries no plan\", strategy, profile)\n112|\t}\n113|\tif err := checkItem(item); err != nil {\n114|\t\treturn Mapping{}, err\n115|\t}\n116|\tdisposition, reasons := baseMapping(strategy, item)\n117|\tdisposition, reasons, err := applyProfile(profile, item, disposition, reasons)\n118|\tif err != nil {\n119|\t\treturn Mapping{}, err\n120|\t}\n121|\tsorted := append([]string(nil), reasons...)\n122|\tsort.Strings(sorted)\n123|\treturn Mapping{Disposition: disposition, Reasons: sorted}, nil\n124|}\n125|\n126|// baseMapping decides the strategy arm: class rules first (opaque\n127|// and aborted history are strategy-independent), then the\n128|// continuation clamp, then the vendor importer degradations, then\n129|// the native exact default.\n130|func baseMapping(strategy string, item Item) (string, []string) {\n131|\tif item.Kind == \"opaque_reasoning\" {\n132|\t\tif item.Protection == protectionSigned {\n133|\t\t\treturn dispositionOpaquePreserved, []string{reasonForeignSigned}\n134|\t\t}\n135|\t\treturn dispositionOpaquePreserved, []string{reasonForeignEncrypted}\n136|\t}\n137|\tif item.Kind == \"opaque_event\" || item.Block == \"opaque\" {\n138|\t\treturn dispositionOpaquePreserved, []string{reasonUnknownNative}\n139|\t}\n140|\tif (item.Kind == \"tool_call\" || item.Kind == \"tool_result\") && item.Resolution == cloneproject.StatusAborted {\n141|\t\treturn dispositionSummarized, []string{reasonUnsafePending}\n142|\t}\n143|\tif strategy == strategyContinuation {\n144|\t\treturn dispositionSemantic, []string{reasonTargetNoEquivalent}\n145|\t}\n146|\tif strategy == strategyOfficial {\n147|\t\tif completeToolKinds[item.Kind] {\n148|\t\t\treturn dispositionSemantic, []string{reasonOfficialImporterLoss}\n149|\t\t}\n150|\t\tif subagentKinds[item.Kind] {\n151|\t\t\treturn dispositionSemantic, []string{reasonGraphFlattened}\n152|\t\t}\n153|\t}\n154|\treturn dispositionExact, nil\n155|}\n156|\n157|// applyProfile refines the strategy mapping under the profile:\n158|// strict_exact refuses non-exact, compact clamps semantic to\n159|// summarized, messages_only omits non-message classes (keeping and\n160|// extending the reason set), and maximal_safe passes through.\n161|func applyProfile(profile string, item Item, disposition string, reasons []string) (string, []string, error) {\n162|\tswitch profile {\n163|\tcase profileStrictExact:\n164|\t\tif disposition != dispositionExact {\n165|\t\t\treturn \"\", nil, invalid(\"projection profile strict_exact refuses %s with disposition %q\", describeItem(item), disposition)\n166|\t\t}\n167|\t\treturn disposition, reasons, nil\n168|\tcase profileCompact:\n169|\t\tif disposition == dispositionSemantic {\n170|\t\t\treturn dispositionSummarized, append(append([]string(nil), reasons...), reasonTargetContextLimit), nil\n171|\t\t}\n172|\t\treturn disposition, reasons, nil\n173|\tcase profileMessages:\n174|\t\tif isMessageClass(item) {\n175|\t\t\treturn disposition, reasons, nil\n176|\t\t}\n177|\t\tomitted := append(append([]string(nil), reasons...), reasonOperatorPolicy)\n178|\t\tif mediaBlocks[item.Block] {\n179|\t\t\tomitted = append(omitted, reasonUnsupportedMedia)\n180|\t\t}\n181|\t\treturn dispositionOmitted, omitted, nil\n182|\tcase profileMaximalSafe:\n183|\t\treturn disposition, reasons, nil\n184|\tdefault:\n185|\t\treturn \"\", nil, invalid(\"projection profile %q is not a target plan profile\", profile)\n186|\t}\n187|}\n188|\n189|// isMessageClass reports whether the item survives messages_only:\n190|// user/assistant message events and text/structured/redacted\n191|// blocks.\n192|func isMessageClass(item Item) bool {\n193|\tif item.Kind != \"\" {\n194|\t\treturn messageKinds[item.Kind]\n195|\t}\n196|\treturn messageBlocks[item.Block]\n197|}\n198|\n199|// describeItem names the item class for refusals.\n200|func describeItem(item Item) string {\n201|\tif item.Kind != \"\" {\n202|\t\treturn \"kind \" + item.Kind\n203|\t}\n204|\treturn \"block \" + item.Block\n205|}\n206|\n207|// PlanSession plans every item in order and folds the predicted\n208|// counts. Sessions are non-empty and bounded by the plan table's\n209|// item_mappings[1..1000000]; the first refusing item refuses the\n210|// session. Counts derive from the mappings, never accepted.\n211|func PlanSession(strategy, profile string, items []Item) ([]Mapping, clonefidelity.FidelityCounts, error) {\n212|\tif len(items) == 0 || len(items) > maxSessionItems {\n213|\t\treturn nil, clonefidelity.FidelityCounts{}, invalid(\"projection session carries %d items, the plan table requires item_mappings[1..1000000]\", len(items))\n214|\t}\n215|\tmappings := make([]Mapping, 0, len(items))\n216|\tvar counts clonefidelity.FidelityCounts\n217|\tfor _, item := range items {\n218|\t\tmapping, err := PlanItem(strategy, profile, item)\n219|\t\tif err != nil {\n220|\t\t\treturn nil, clonefidelity.FidelityCounts{}, err\n221|\t\t}\n222|\t\tmappings = append(mappings, mapping)\n223|\t\tswitch mapping.Disposition {\n224|\t\tcase dispositionExact:\n225|\t\t\tcounts.Exact++\n226|\t\tcase dispositionSemantic:\n227|\t\t\tcounts.Semantic++\n228|\t\tcase dispositionSummarized:\n229|\t\t\tcounts.Summarized++\n230|\t\tcase dispositionOpaquePreserved:\n231|\t\t\tcounts.OpaquePreserved++\n232|\t\tcase dispositionOmitted:\n233|\t\t\tcounts.Omitted++\n234|\t\tdefault:\n235|\t\t\treturn nil, clonefidelity.FidelityCounts{}, invalid(\"projection session planned unexpected disposition %q\", mapping.Disposition)\n236|\t\t}\n237|\t}\n238|\treturn mappings, counts, nil\n239|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c657","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":390,"recorded_at":1780531400000775,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"call_id":"call_01a0d33ede4f7358aa8997ff829f703e","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneplanning/effects.go`.\n1|package cloneplanning\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonefidelity\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// This file folds planned mappings to target effects: callable\n8|// tools, pending actions, and target token accounting. Historical\n9|// tools are inert and source usage is not target accounting\n10|// (Section 13.14.1), so the fold is always empty: no mapping admits\n11|// a live effect. Mappings carry no token field by type, so token\n12|// counts cannot reach the accounting decision at all; the sweep\n13|// proves every mapping the planner emits folds to zero.\n14|\n15|// TargetEffects is the planned session's live surface: callable\n16|// tools, pending actions, and target token accounting. Planning\n17|// from captured history always yields the zero value.\n18|type TargetEffects struct {\n19|\tCallableTools      []string\n20|\tPendingActions     []string\n21|\tTargetInputTokens  uint64\n22|\tTargetOutputTokens uint64\n23|}\n24|\n25|// PlanTargetEffects folds planned mappings to their target\n26|// effects: always empty. Every mapping is validated first (closed\n27|// disposition, vocabulary reasons in sorted-unique order), so\n28|// garbage mappings refuse instead of folding.\n29|func PlanTargetEffects(mappings []Mapping) (TargetEffects, error) {\n30|\tfor index, mapping := range mappings {\n31|\t\tif !clonefidelity.ValidDisposition(mapping.Disposition) {\n32|\t\t\treturn TargetEffects{}, invalid(\"target effects mapping[%d] disposition %q is outside the Section 13.14.2 vocabulary\", index, mapping.Disposition)\n33|\t\t}\n34|\t\tfor _, reason := range mapping.Reasons {\n35|\t\t\tif !clonefidelity.ValidReasonCode(reason) {\n36|\t\t\t\treturn TargetEffects{}, invalid(\"target effects mapping[%d] reason %q is not a core or reverse-DNS reason\", index, reason)\n37|\t\t\t}\n38|\t\t}\n39|\t\tfor position := 1; position < len(mapping.Reasons); position++ {\n40|\t\t\tif mapping.Reasons[position-1] >= mapping.Reasons[position] {\n41|\t\t\t\treturn TargetEffects{}, invalid(\"target effects mapping[%d] reasons are not sorted unique\", index)\n42|\t\t\t}\n43|\t\t}\n44|\t}\n45|\treturn TargetEffects{}, nil\n46|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
