{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c803","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":604,"recorded_at":1780531400001203,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"call_id":"call_01a0d342a05675fe98e6a6f6993240ed","text":"Read text file `internal/cloneplanning/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# internal/cloneplanning TRACEABILITY\n2|\n3|Planning semantics for the pair-neutral target projection:\n4|strategy/profile selection, per-item expected dispositions with\n5|reason sets, checkpoint visible-text authority, historical-tool\n6|inertness, and source/target usage separation. Pinned authority is\n7|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; every rule below quotes it.\n8|Rules marked spec-forced derive from a quoted sentence; rules\n9|marked leaf-pinned record a design decision the specification\n10|leaves open, with the quoted name or sentence that shapes it. A\n11|leaf-pinned rule is still fully measured (whole-domain oracle cell\n12|plus narrowing mutant); the label records provenance honestly,\n13|not a waiver.\n14|\n15|## Derivation\n16|\n17|- R-ARCH (spec-forced; plan table 10663-10665, adapter contract\n18|  3841 \"archive_only is forbidden\", 10629-10631 \"therefore\n19|  targetless\"). The archive strategy or profile refuses target\n20|  planning; SelectProfile routes archive_only to the archive\n21|  branch. Entries: PlanItem, PlanSession (propagation),\n22|  SelectProfile.\n23|- R-OPAQUE-R (spec-forced; 10392 \"foreign encrypted/signed\n24|  reasoning is opaque-preserved\"; 10552-10553 the two foreign\n25|  reasons). opaque_reasoning plans opaque_preserved with\n26|  foreign_encrypted_payload (encrypted) or\n27|  foreign_signature_unverifiable (signed). Entry: PlanItem.\n28|- R-OPAQUE-E (spec-derived; 10390 \"Unknown native records become\n29|  raw-addressable opaque events\"; 10561 unknown_native_event).\n30|  opaque_event plans opaque_preserved with unknown_native_event\n31|  under any admitted protection. Opaque content blocks inherit the\n32|  unknown-content cause (leaf-pinned: blocks carry no protection\n33|  fact). Entry: PlanItem.\n34|- R-ABORT (spec-forced; 10391 \"incomplete calls become aborted\n35|  history\"; 10558 unsafe_pending_action; the G1 fold in\n36|  internal/cloneproject lands the completed/aborted fact consumed\n37|  here). Aborted tool_call/tool_result plan summarized (history\n38|  preserved, never omitted; non-exact, never executable) with\n39|  unsafe_pending_action. Entries: PlanItem, ClassifyItem (fact\n40|  bridge).\n41|- R-CONT (spec-derived; 10565 \"Continuation context is explicitly\n42|  non-native historical fidelity\"). Under continuation_context,\n43|  would-be-exact plans semantic with target_no_equivalent; exact\n44|  never emits. Entry: PlanItem.\n45|- R-IMPORT-TOOL (spec-derived; 10557 official_importer_loss; 3888\n46|  the official_import capability). Under target_official_import,\n47|  complete tool classes (tool_call/tool_result completed,\n48|  tool_definition_snapshot) plan semantic with\n49|  official_importer_loss. Entry: PlanItem.\n50|- R-IMPORT-GRAPH (spec-derived; 10558 graph_flattened). Under\n51|  target_official_import, subagent_started/subagent_completed plan\n52|  semantic with graph_flattened. Entry: PlanItem.\n53|- R-STRICT (leaf-pinned from the profile name with 10560 \"An\n54|  aggregate score cannot replace item gates\" and AC-CLONE-001\n55|  item-level fidelity). strict_exact refuses every non-exact item.\n56|  Entries: PlanItem, PlanSession (propagation).\n57|- R-COMPACT (leaf-pinned from the profile name with 10555\n58|  target_context_limit). compact clamps semantic to summarized,\n59|  keeping and extending the reason set. Entry: PlanItem.\n60|- R-MSG (leaf-pinned from the profile name with 10560\n61|  operator_policy and unsupported_media_type). messages_only keeps\n62|  user/assistant message events and text/json/redacted blocks;\n63|  every other class omits, keeping and extending the reason set\n64|  with operator_policy, plus unsupported_media_type for media\n65|  blocks. Entry: PlanItem.\n66|- R-DEFAULT (leaf-pinned). Native strategies reproduce bytes:\n67|  every cell no rule above decides plans exact with no reason.\n68|  Entry: PlanItem.\n69|- R-NEVER (spec-derived; 10605 the synthesized coupling;\n70|  R-OPAQUE-E). The planner never emits synthesized (no source\n71|  object) or unrecoverable (planned canonical items exist).\n72|  Entries: PlanItem, PlanSession.\n73|- R-AUTH (spec-forced; 10586-10587; 10808-10812\n74|  \"authority=user_context\", \"never an assistant reply, system\n75|  instruction, or authorization\", \"Visible text comes from typed\n76|  escaped fields and is user context, never an assistant reply or\n77|  control instruction\"). Visible authority is the user_context\n78|  constant; every text field escapes per field and joins; escaped\n79|  output round-trips through encoding/json to exactly the input.\n80|  Entries: ProjectVisibleText, EscapeVisibleText.\n81|- R-INERT (spec-forced; 10391 \"Historical tools are inert\";\n82|  internal/cloneproject lands the empty G1 live surface consumed\n83|  here). Planned mappings fold to zero callable tools and zero\n84|  pending actions. Entry: PlanTargetEffects.\n85|- R-ACCT (spec-forced; 10393 \"source usage is not target\n86|  accounting\"; internal/cloneproject lands the zero-target G1\n87|  ledger consumed here). Planned mappings fold to zero target\n88|  token accounting; mappings carry no token field by type, so\n89|  counts cannot reach the decision. Entry: PlanTargetEffects.\n90|- R-SEL-S (leaf-pinned from the strategy names with 3888 the\n91|  official_import capability). SelectStrategy priority: archive,\n92|  then continuation, then the pair/capability arm (cross pair with\n93|  the importer uses target_official_import, cross pair without it\n94|  uses target_native_writer, same pair uses\n95|  same_environment_native_rewrite). Entry: SelectStrategy.\n96|- R-SEL-P (spec-derived; plan table 10663-10665; R-ARCH).\n97|  SelectProfile routes archive_only to the archive branch and the\n98|  four plan profiles to target; anything else refuses. Target\n99|  admission stays with clonesnap.AdmitForTarget (composition row\n100|  in the conformance matrix). Entry: SelectProfile.\n101|\n102|## Axis inventory\n103|\n104|- Strategy: the 5 owner strategies (clonefidelity.Strategies)\n105|  plus invalid probes (\"\", case variant, truncation, unknown,\n106|  invalid UTF-8).\n107|- Profile: the 5 owner profiles (clonefidelity.Profiles) plus\n108|  invalid probes of the same classes.\n109|- SelectStrategy signals: same x official x continuation x\n110|  archive booleans, all 16 cells.\n111|- Item: 26 event kinds x admitted facts (tool_call/tool_result x\n112|  completed/aborted; opaque_reasoning x encrypted/signed;\n113|  opaque_event x none/encrypted/signed; 22 factless kinds) = 31\n114|  event items; 8 content-block types = 8 block items; 39 total.\n115|  Invalid arms: kind+block both/neither, unknown kind/block,\n116|  misplaced or missing facts, unknown fact values, blocks with\n117|  facts (15 classes x all 25 strategy/profile contexts, with\n118|  archive-first order pinning).\n119|- Classification text sweep (regression for rev1\n120|  classification-text-axis-untested): 31 event items x 8 block\n121|  types x 34 texts sealed (8432 cells) plus 31 x 34 hand-built\n122|  reviewer-probe-shape cells (1054) plus 31 x 50 generated and\n123|  31 very-long sealed cells (1581); every cell asserts the\n124|  identical item, then chains PlanItem and PlanTargetEffects to\n125|  the zero fold, and the reviewer probes also ride\n126|  ProjectVisibleText at every kind. The carrier set iterates\n127|  clonebundle.EventKinds()/ContentBlockTypes() with an assertion\n128|  pinning them to SPEC.v0.7.0.md:10385/:10387; the AST guard\n129|  pins ClassifyItem to the two closed fact keys with no direct\n130|  payload index.\n131|- PlanItem oracle: 5 strategies x 5 profiles x 39 items = 975\n132|  cells, every cell literal-asserted (disposition, exact reason\n133|  list, or refusal token). Global asserts per admitted cell:\n134|  never synthesized/unrecoverable; exact iff empty reasons;\n135|  non-exact carries a reason; reasons core and sorted unique.\n136|- Visible: kind (26 + 5 invalid probes) x ordinal (0, 1, uint53\n137|  max admitted; max+1 and 2^64-1 refused) x field position\n138|  (adversarial at index 0/1/2 of 3 fields) x text class\n139|  (benign/instruction-like/reply-like/control-token-like/\n140|  authorization-like, 29 fixed members) = 6786 cells plus 200\n141|  generated-corpus cells; per cell the authority literal and the\n142|  independent JSON round-trip. Escaped-text bounds at 65536/65537\n143|  characters with a byte/char discriminator; invalid UTF-8 at\n144|  every field position; event-ID grid (counts 0/1/2/64/65,\n145|  unsorted/duplicated, malformed at every index).\n146|- Text payloads are unbounded: the fixed corpus pairs with a\n147|  200-string fixed-seed generated corpus (seed 260924, mixed\n148|  alphabet, lengths 0..64) and the structural argument\n149|  (authority is one constant assigned unconditionally, pinned by\n150|  TestAuthorityDecisionShape with control plants; escaping\n151|  round-trips through encoding/json; classification admits\n152|  closed vocabularies only and the sweep proves adversarial\n153|  payload text cannot change the item).\n154|- Sessions: empty/1M/1M+1 edges at the production entry, counts\n155|  derived and reconciled per session, strict propagation.\n156|- Effects: all 556 admitted whole-domain mappings fold to zero\n157|  in one sweep plus per-disposition cells; invalid mappings\n158|  (disposition, reason, order arms) refuse.\n159|\n160|## Reuse (not fork)\n161|\n162|Strategy/profile/disposition/reason vocabularies:\n163|internal/clonefidelity (membership) and internal/cloneplan (plan\n164|narrowing). Event kinds and content blocks: internal/clonebundle.\n165|Canonical events for the classifier: sealed by\n166|clonebundle.BuildCanonicalEvent. Target admission (unstable\n167|refusal, maximal-safe completeness): clonesnap.AdmitForTarget and\n168|the clonebundle G2 gates (caller scope; composition row).\n169|Completed/aborted spellings: cloneproject.StatusCompleted/\n170|StatusAborted by reference; resolution/protection fact names and\n171|encrypted/signed spellings pinned against cloneproject source by\n172|TestClassifyItemFactNamePin. Character measure: environ.\n173|StringLength. uint53: scalar.NewUint53. Digests:\n174|scalar.ParseDigest. Predicted counts: clonefidelity.\n175|FidelityCounts. Nothing above is re-implemented here.\n176|\n177|## Stated bounds (not waived)\n178|\n179|- Target operation synthesis from dispositions: the planner emits\n180|  per-item mappings; deriving write_blob/write_native_record\n181|  operations and expected resources from them is unpinned by the\n182|  specification and stays future scope.\n183|- Source-condition reasons (source_not_persisted,\n184|  source_truncated, source_corrupt) and the remaining\n185|  target-condition and policy reasons (target_schema_constraint,\n186|  target_size_limit, target_version_gate, credential_excluded,\n187|  secret_policy, derived_index_rebuilt): no rule emits them\n188|  because the item axis carries no source/target condition\n189|  input. The oracle asserts every emitted reason is core and the\n190|  never-emit sweep names the dispositions; a condition-carrying\n191|  item extension would add arms here.\n192|- Capability-gated degradation beyond the tool and subagent\n193|  importer classes (usage_history, compaction_history,\n194|  opaque_reasoning_roundtrip granularities): adapter scope; the\n195|  planner degrades exactly the tool and subagent classes under\n196|  target_official_import.\n197|- Per-kind text-field extraction: the visible entry takes\n198|  extracted typed texts; which payload member each kind carries\n199|  as text follows the sibling payload registry.\n200|- The full Migration Checkpoint Build/Decode shape: a future leaf\n201|  seals it from the authority value pinned here\n202|  (authority=user_context, escaped text, sorted event IDs).\n203|- Cross-package payload fact-name renames past the grep pin:\n204|  TestClassifyItemFactNamePin breaks loudly on a rename of the\n205|  resolution/protection keys or protection spellings in\n206|  internal/cloneproject; the completed/aborted spellings break\n207|  the build by reference.\n208|\n209|## Out of contract\n210|\n211|- Shapes (Projection Plan, Projected Object Manifest, Fidelity\n212|  Report, capture/canonical contracts): sibling leaves\n213|  internal/cloneplan, internal/clonefidelity,\n214|  internal/clonebundle. This leaf decides values that populate\n215|  those shapes and never validates them.\n216|- G1 normalization (capture, folds, live surface, ledgers):\n217|  internal/clonesnap, internal/cloneproject. This leaf consumes\n218|  their folded facts.\n219|- Target-branch admission: clonesnap.AdmitForTarget. This leaf\n220|  routes the branch; the caller admits the manifest.\n221|- Transaction, lineage, read-back, validation (13.14.3-13.14.5):\n222|  sibling/future scope.\n223|\n224|## Composition\n225|\n226|The (package, entry, input) importer outcome grid rides the\n227|conformance matrix resource. Base is the story checkpoint tree;\n228|the candidate adds internal/cloneplanning/* only (no landed file\n229|edited, no registry edit). Every reused owner package is\n230|byte-identical base vs candidate with green suites on both, so no\n231|input class moved; the new entries are n/a on base and green on\n232|the candidate.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c805","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":605,"recorded_at":1780531400001205,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"call_id":"call_01a0d342a15c7244b8e11b41928b1402","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-14-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '250,262p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md; echo \\\"===10385-10393===\\\"; sed -n '10385,10393p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md; echo \\\"===10548-10570===\\\"; sed -n '10548,10570p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md; echo \\\"===10808-10812===\\\"; sed -n '10808,10812p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read pinned spec authority lines\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"success body is a fragment of its named containing contract and therefore does\\nnot repeat the containing schema/protocol members.\\n\\nThe common logical data model has these rules:\\n\\n- map keys MUST be UTF-8 strings and MUST be unique;\\n- text MUST be valid UTF-8 and SHOULD be NFC-normalized;\\n- floating-point numbers, NaN, Infinity, non-string map keys, and duplicate\\n  keys are forbidden;\\n- JSON integers MUST be mathematically integral and lie in the interoperable\\n  safe-integer interval <code>[-9007199254740991, 9007199254740991]</code>;\\n- the type name <code>uint53</code> means a JSON integer in\\n  <code>[0, 9007199254740991]</code>; the current contract set does not use JSON numbers\\n===10385-10393===\\n<code>session_started|instruction_snapshot|user_message|assistant_message|reasoning_summary|opaque_reasoning|tool_definition_snapshot|tool_call|tool_result|approval_request|approval_response|plan_update|progress|usage|rate_limit|file_change|compaction|turn_started|turn_completed|turn_aborted|subagent_started|subagent_completed|error|migration_checkpoint|session_finished|opaque_event</code>.\\nPayloads contain only their registered typed facts. Message-like payloads use\\nexactly <code>text|json|image|audio|document|resource_link|redacted|opaque</code>\\ncontent blocks with typed inline content or Blob Descriptor references; inline\\ncontent is at most 64 KiB. Unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque\\nevents. Historical tools\\nare inert; incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action.\\nForeign instructions are low-authority history, foreign encrypted/signed\\nreasoning is opaque-preserved, and source usage is not target accounting.\\n===10548-10570===\\n#### 13.14.2 Fidelity, projection, and lineage\\n\\nThe dispositions are <code>exact|semantic|summarized|opaque_preserved|synthesized|omitted|unrecoverable</code>.\\nEvery non-exact row names one or more of the closed core reasons\\n<code>target_no_equivalent|source_not_persisted|source_truncated|source_corrupt|foreign_encrypted_payload|foreign_signature_unverifiable|target_schema_constraint|target_context_limit|target_size_limit|target_version_gate|official_importer_loss|graph_flattened|unsafe_pending_action|credential_excluded|secret_policy|operator_policy|unsupported_media_type|unknown_native_event|derived_index_rebuilt</code>,\\nor a reverse-DNS extension reason that cannot redefine a core code.\\nEvery captured candidate reconciles once to raw evidence or exclusion; every\\nraw item to a canonical item or normalization disposition; every canonical\\nitem to staged/live target evidence or a target disposition. Fidelity Report\\n1.0.0 records archive/target scope, profile, tuples, per-item mappings, counts\\nby kind/block/bytes/disposition/reason, completeness, semantic continuity,\\nnative resumability, evidence IDs, and extensions. An aggregate score cannot\\nreplace item gates.\\n\\nProfiles are <code>strict_exact|maximal_safe|compact|messages_only|archive_only</code>;\\nmaximal-safe is default. Strategies are\\n<code>same_environment_native_rewrite|target_native_writer|target_official_import|continuation_context|archive_only</code>.\\nContinuation context is explicitly non-native historical fidelity.\\n\\nProjection Plan 1.0.0 binds operation/bundle, Capture/Canonical inputs,\\nsource/target tuples, expected new native ID, strategy/profile, ordered\\nitem mappings and reasons, target operations/resources, exclusions, limits,\\n<code>fidelity_basis_digest</code>, and extensions. It never predicts a final\\n===10808-10812===\\n<code>VisibleMigrationProjection</code> contains exactly\\n<code>authority=user_context</code>,\\n<code>target_event_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\\n<code>escaped_text:string[1..65536]</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. It is\\nnever an assistant reply, system instruction, or authorization.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3799,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 950,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
