{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c913","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d33e-21a1-7dd1-8410-6ee446430389"},"sequence":740,"recorded_at":1780531400001475,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4e561a79-c0d9-4ce2-8e43-bf7439b5274c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d343-206e-7831-8cad-43e7284e5383"},"task_id":"01a0d343-206e-7831-8cad-43e7284e5383","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d343-206e-7831-8cad-43e7284e5383","chunk":"Read text file `.temp/rev3/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260924-3n78rv results (rev2): projection planning and authority rules\n2|\n3|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED tree in the STORY-260830-21bxa3 worktree\n4|(`internal/cloneplanning/*`, 17 new paths only; no landed file\n5|edited, no registry edit). Change Request is `task_delta`. This\n6|revision answers CR rev1 verdict `classification-text-axis-untested`\n7|with a named regression test plus two narrowing mutants, and\n8|`stale-trunk-candidate` via a single end-of-work\n9|`refresh-candidate`: `refresh_advanced` to trunk `6d3bff9`\n10|(branch `618d78d`), trunk-ancestor verified, 81/81 trunk-only\n11|non-board paths blob-equal to trunk, worktree synced (all prior\n12|tracked diffs were stale pre-refresh blobs, zero live edits), and\n13|tree-bound validation rerun green on the refreshed tree.\n14|\n15|Rework delta (rev1 -> rev2): new\n16|`internal/cloneplanning/classification_allkinds_test.go` (all-kinds\n17|adversarial sweep derived from `clonebundle.EventKinds()` /\n18|`ContentBlockTypes()` with a spec-line assertion, plus an AST\n19|guard pinning `ClassifyItem` to the two closed fact keys); two new\n20|harness rows (`N-classify-text-subagent`, the reviewer's exact\n21|plant, and `N-classify-text-usage`); one TRACEABILITY axis bullet.\n22|No production file changed.\n23|\n24|## AC coverage, measured: 18 of 18 rows driven\n25|\n26|Row 12 is now fully driven (rev1 verdict measured 17/18 with row\n27|12 partial at `ClassifyItem`). Each row names its production call\n28|site; every refusal is literal-pinned and every gate carries a\n29|killed narrowing (matrix names them).\n30|\n31|| # | Row | Call site | Test |\n32||---|---|---|---|\n33|| 1 | Strategy selection, 16 cells | SS | TestSelectStrategyOracle |\n34|| 2 | Profile branch routing, 5 + invalids | SP | TestSelectProfileOracle |\n35|| 3 | Item dispositions + reasons, 975 cells | PI | TestPlanItemWholeDomainOracle + 8 rule tests |\n36|| 4 | Archive refusal with branch message | PI, SP | TestPlanItemArchiveRule, TestSelectProfileOracle |\n37|| 5 | Continuation never exact | PI | TestPlanItemContinuationRule |\n38|| 6 | Opaque reasons by protection/cause | PI | TestPlanItemOpaqueRule |\n39|| 7 | Aborted tools are summarized history | PI, CI | TestPlanItemAbortRule, TestClassifyItemValidGrid |\n40|| 8 | Importer tool loss + graph flattening | PI | TestPlanItemImporterRule |\n41|| 9 | Strict/compact/messages overlays | PI | TestPlanItemStrictRule, TestPlanItemCompactRule, TestPlanItemMessagesRule |\n42|| 10 | Visible authority always user_context | PV | TestProjectVisibleWholeDomain (6986 cells) |\n43|| 11 | Escaping round-trips via encoding/json | PV, EV | TestProjectVisibleWholeDomain, TestProjectVisibleEscapingOracle |\n44|| 12 | Adversarial text never gains authority (every kind x every block type x every text class x every entry) | CI, PI, TE, PV | TestClassifyItemIgnoresPayloadTextAllKinds (8432 sealed + 1054 hand-built + 1581 generated/long, downstream chain to zero, reviewer probes through PV); TestClassifyItemReadsClosedFactsOnly (AST); TestClassifyItemVocabMatchesSpec (spec pin); TestProjectVisibleWholeDomain, TestProjectVisiblePositionIndependence; SS/SP/PI/PS/TE take no text by type |\n45|| 13 | Tools inert; pending blocked | TE, PI | TestPlanTargetEffectsZeroSweep, TestPlanTargetEffectsChained |\n46|| 14 | Source usage never target accounting | TE | TestPlanTargetEffectsZeroSweep (556 mappings + per-disposition) |\n47|| 15 | Token classes (control-token text + usage counts) | PV, TE | rows 11 + 14 probes |\n48|| 16 | Vendor importer strategy arm | PI | TestPlanItemImporterRule |\n49|| 17 | Session counts + empty/1M/1M+1 edges | PS | TestPlanSessionCounts, TestPlanSessionRefusals, TestPlanSessionMillionEdge |\n50|| 18 | Importer grid base vs candidate, moved classes named | — | owners.log, byte-identity (232 files, 0 differ, moved none) |\n51|\n52|Stated bounds (not waived): operation synthesis; source/target\n53|condition reasons outside the item axis; capability-gated\n54|degradation past tool/subagent importer classes; per-kind\n55|text-field extraction (visible entry takes extracted typed texts);\n56|full Migration Checkpoint sealing; fact-name renames past the\n57|grep pin. See TRACEABILITY.md.\n58|\n59|## Out-of-contract rows (declared, not silent)\n60|\n61|- Closed shapes (plan, manifest, fidelity report, capture,\n62|  canonical): sibling leaves cloneplan/clonefidelity/clonebundle;\n63|  this leaf decides populating values, never validates shapes.\n64|- G1 normalization and folds: clonesnap/cloneproject; consumed\n65|  here by reference and source pin.\n66|- Target-branch admission: clonesnap.AdmitForTarget (caller\n67|  scope); this leaf routes the branch only.\n68|- Transaction, lineage, read-back, validation (13.14.3-13.14.5):\n69|  sibling/future scope.\n70|\n71|## Brief gap (handoff precondition 1)\n72|\n73|The brief carries no surface table, so there is no surface row to\n74|map. Coverage map substitute: the clause map in\n75|`internal/cloneplanning/TRACEABILITY.md` maps every derivation\n76|rule to its production entries and named tests, and the\n77|conformance matrix maps every gate to its entries, killer tests,\n78|and killed narrowings (50 narrowings + 1 control).\n79|\n80|## Reviewer tests kept\n81|\n82|No previously committed reviewer test exists on the board (rev1\n83|verdict carried probe files inside its evidence tar, not committed\n84|tests). The reviewer's exact `subagent_started` plant and all six\n85|probe texts are now embedded in the committed sweep\n86|(`reviewerShortProbes`, `reviewerLongProbe`) and harness row\n87|`N-classify-text-subagent`, so the next cycle inherits them.\n88|\n89|## Validation (real exit codes)\n90|\n91|| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n92||---|---|---|\n93|| `go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplanning/ -v` | 0 | `package.log` |\n94|| `go test -count=1 -cover ./internal/cloneplanning/` | 0, 97.8% statements | (run output) |\n95|| `go test -count=3` on the 3 new tests | 0 | `determinism.log` |\n96|| `go test -p 2 -count=1 ./...` (full suite pre-refresh, bounded parallelism) | 0, 47 ok, 0 FAIL | `full.log` |\n97|| Post-refresh: package, 9 owners, vet, windows-vet, build, hygiene | 0 all | `package-postrefresh.log`, `owners-postrefresh.log`, `vet-postrefresh.log`, `winvet-postrefresh.log`, `build-postrefresh.log`, `hygiene-postrefresh.log` |\n98|| Mutant battery, 51 rows, post-refresh run | 50 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness3-summary.log`, `harness3/` |\n99|| `go test -p 2 -count=1 ./...` (full suite post-refresh, bounded parallelism) | 0, 48 ok, 0 FAIL | `full-postrefresh.log` |\n100|| `go vet ./...` | 0 | `vet.log` |\n101|| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` | 0 | `winvet.log` |\n102|| `gofmt -l internal` | 0, no files | `gofmt.log` |\n103|| `go build ./...` | 0 | `build.log` |\n104|| Mutant battery, 51 rows, run 1 | 50 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness1-summary.log`, `harness1/` |\n105|| Mutant battery, 51 rows, run 2 | 50 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness2-summary.log`, `harness2/` |\n106|| Old 5-carrier test on the subagent plant (gap repro) | 0 SURVIVED | `old-test-survives-subagent.log` |\n107|| New all-kinds test on the subagent plant (kill) | 1,