gs + per-disposition) |\n47|| 15 | Token classes (control-token text + usage counts) | PV, TE | rows 11 + 14 probes |\n48|| 16 | Vendor importer strategy arm | PI | TestPlanItemImporterRule |\n49|| 17 | Session counts + empty/1M/1M+1 edges | PS | TestPlanSessionCounts, TestPlanSessionRefusals, TestPlanSessionMillionEdge |\n50|| 18 | Importer grid base vs candidate, moved classes named | — | owners.log, byte-identity (232 files, 0 differ, moved none) |\n51|\n52|Stated bounds (not waived): operation synthesis; source/target\n53|condition reasons outside the item axis; capability-gated\n54|degradation past tool/subagent importer classes; per-kind\n55|text-field extraction (visible entry takes extracted typed texts);\n56|full Migration Checkpoint sealing; fact-name renames past the\n57|grep pin. See TRACEABILITY.md.\n58|\n59|## Out-of-contract rows (declared, not silent)\n60|\n61|- Closed shapes (plan, manifest, fidelity report, capture,\n62|  canonical): sibling leaves cloneplan/clonefidelity/clonebundle;\n63|  this leaf decides populating values, never validates shapes.\n64|- G1 normalization and folds: clonesnap/cloneproject; consumed\n65|  here by reference and source pin.\n66|- Target-branch admission: clonesnap.AdmitForTarget (caller\n67|  scope); this leaf routes the branch only.\n68|- Transaction, lineage, read-back, validation (13.14.3-13.14.5):\n69|  sibling/future scope.\n70|\n71|## Brief gap (handoff precondition 1)\n72|\n73|The brief carries no surface table, so there is no surface row to\n74|map. Coverage map substitute: the clause map in\n75|`internal/cloneplanning/TRACEABILITY.md` maps every derivation\n76|rule to its production entries and named tests, and the\n77|conformance matrix maps every gate to its entries, killer tests,\n78|and killed narrowings (50 narrowings + 1 control).\n79|\n80|## Reviewer tests kept\n81|\n82|No previously committed reviewer test exists on the board (rev1\n83|verdict carried probe files inside its evidence tar, not committed\n84|tests). The reviewer's exact `subagent_started` plant and all six\n85|probe texts are now embedded in the committed sweep\n86|(`reviewerShortProbes`, `reviewerLongProbe`) and harness row\n87|`N-classify-text-subagent`, so the next cycle inherits them.\n88|\n89|## Validation (real exit codes)\n90|\n91|| Command | Exit | Evidence |\n92||---|---|---|\n93|| `go test -count=1 ./internal/cloneplanning/ -v` | 0 | `package.log` |\n94|| `go test -count=1 -cover ./internal/cloneplanning/` | 0, 97.8% statements | (run output) |\n95|| `go test -count=3` on the 3 new tests | 0 | `determinism.log` |\n96|| `go test -p 2 -count=1 ./...` (full suite pre-refresh, bounded parallelism) | 0, 47 ok, 0 FAIL | `full.log` |\n97|| Post-refresh: package, 9 owners, vet, windows-vet, build, hygiene | 0 all | `package-postrefresh.log`, `owners-postrefresh.log`, `vet-postrefresh.log`, `winvet-postrefresh.log`, `build-postrefresh.log`, `hygiene-postrefresh.log` |\n98|| Mutant battery, 51 rows, post-refresh run | 50 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness3-summary.log`, `harness3/` |\n99|| `go test -p 2 -count=1 ./...` (full suite post-refresh, bounded parallelism) | 0, 48 ok, 0 FAIL | `full-postrefresh.log` |\n100|| `go vet ./...` | 0 | `vet.log` |\n101|| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` | 0 | `winvet.log` |\n102|| `gofmt -l internal` | 0, no files | `gofmt.log` |\n103|| `go build ./...` | 0 | `build.log` |\n104|| Mutant battery, 51 rows, run 1 | 50 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness1-summary.log`, `harness1/` |\n105|| Mutant battery, 51 rows, run 2 | 50 KILLED + control SURVIVED, 0 mismatches | `harness2-summary.log`, `harness2/` |\n106|| Old 5-carrier test on the subagent plant (gap repro) | 0 SURVIVED | `old-test-survives-subagent.log` |\n107|| New all-kinds test on the subagent plant (kill) | 1, flip named | `new-test-kills-subagent.log` |\n108|| AST guard on direct-index control (must redden) | 1, index named | `ast-control-a.log` |\n109|| AST guard on